         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/614760fe-cfd8-4ef2-a1df-d57159716759,1794349811063/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%2813%2C0%2C3367%2C1893%29%3B' alt='A map of the planned Ontario Line with 15 stops from Exhibition to Don Valley Station.' width='620' height='349' title=''/><p>The Ontario Line has hit a major milestone: a tunnel boring machine has drilled through more than a kilometre of bedrock to reach the site of the future King West station. CBC’s Mercedes Gaztambide explores what this means — and when commuters can actually expect to ride it.</p>]]></description>
